    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-perspective-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Frame an inference or attribute a viewpoint",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "看来 introduces an inference from what is apparent. 在 + person + 看来 attributes a judgment to that person. Both mark a viewpoint rather than establish a fact. 一般来说 marks a generalization that can admit exceptions.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "看来今天没开门。",
                "pinyin": "kànlái jīntiān méi kāi mén 。",
                "meaning": "It looks as though it is closed today.",
                "audio": "8005378877640fee09ccde3dc65dc3ad94861f9ce4ad27adf8308cfb9a00c870"
              },
              {
                "text": "在他看来，新书总比旧书好。",
                "pinyin": "zài tā kànlái ， xīn shū zǒng bǐ jiù shū hǎo 。",
                "meaning": "In his view, new books are always better than old books.",
                "audio": "21624014f71f1dec755d754fcc4c4e055d3daaf0f25020482c94aa0431b352ba"
              },
              {
                "text": "一般来说，这里的冬天很冷。",
                "pinyin": "yībān láishuō ， zhèlǐ de dōngtiān hěn lěng 。",
                "meaning": "Generally speaking, winters here are cold.",
                "audio": "55a5daebc9f6989c70a48b734cf0b99a6b037baf188e670e4e1817364e4ffa95"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
